r but I was there in the late afternoon and saw all that I needed to.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2013-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "872345818FD58D47753E636E70FF0CCD", "name": "sundevilfanMesa", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sundevilfanMesa", "username": "sundevilfanMesa", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/b8/default-avatar-2020-26.jpg", "contribution_count": 17, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 31281, "location_name": "Mesa", "location_name_detailed": "Mesa, Arizona"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-25", "published_at_date": "2013-04-25"}, {"review_id": 158771200, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158771200-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A magical experience.", "text": "Visit in the evening at about 18.30pm. Each night there is a celebratory/ mystical and musical ceremony to worship Lord Shiva. It is a spine tingling experience, never to be forgotten. The celebration lasts for about an hour. I have always found the Hindu participants so welcoming to visitors. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2013-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CA2B00E7258AACEE2A31DD296873A192", "name": "56Anna", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/56Anna", "username": "56Anna", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/e3/default-avatar-2020-59.jpg", "contribution_count": 52, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 209940, "location_name": "Skipton", "location_name_detailed": "Skipton, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-25", "published_at_date": "2013-04-25"}, {"review_id": 158750406, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158750406-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very moving place", "text": "A sacred Hindu place and very moving with the cremations happening right in front of you. I visited all the major attractions in Kathmandu and found hear and boudanath stupa the two best.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "21A1A66CE922434E00E4B7B5D4AD516F", "name": "MatthewSurawski", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/MatthewSurawski", "username": "MatthewSurawski", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3e/a1/7e/matthewsurawski.jpg", "contribution_count": 127, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 2663383, "location_name": "Aratula", "location_name_detailed": "Aratula, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-25", "published_at_date": "2013-04-25"}, {"review_id": 158725307, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158725307-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Heaven for Hindus", "text": "Excellent temple, Very sacred for Hindus Beware the temple is right next to cremation ground. the view of cremation ground may disturb a lot  of people and children so better stay away from the outer boundry of temple. Other then that very nice place", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2013-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "A3421669A664487D2B10E24D52953CD5", "name": "ecimadh", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ecimadh", "username": "ecimadh", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/4a/b2/f1/ecimadh.jpg", "contribution_count": 60, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297615, "location_name": "Gurugram (Gurgaon)", "location_name_detailed": "Gurugram (Gurgaon), India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-25", "published_at_date": "2013-04-24"}, {"review_id": 158601497, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158601497-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Conflicting", "text": "I visited Pashupatinath as part of a day long UNESCO heritage site tour. Of the four major sites we visited this was my least favorite. It is a very holy place for Hindus and is where all cremations in Kathmandu for Hindus take place. Please note these cremations are visible and in the open air. Bring a scarf or mask with you. You will 95% sure see at least one cremation. On the day we were there there were four occurring when we walked in. Non-Hindus cannot enter the temple and most end up staying on one side of the complex. I have been to a lot of holy places of all sorts of different religions before and this one didn't have the feeling like a holy place. It felt like it was a neglected place where people are easily taken advantage of. There are also \"sadhus\" sitting around and will let you take a picture for a price. It just overall had a negative feeling to me. I kept trying to see and feel why it was holy but I couldn't. You will also most likely get hassled from the street all the way to the temple complex by people selling things. If you go I would plan to spend less than a half hour here.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4F5E0608F5B8A679350D13F3FAC4912E", "name": "ihavethewanders", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ihavethewanders", "username": "ihavethewanders", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/75/f9/38/rahrah22.jpg", "contribution_count": 123, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60745, "location_name": "Boston", "location_name_detailed": "Boston, Massachusetts"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-23", "published_at_date": "2013-04-23"}, {"review_id": 158428775, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158428775-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "It's right next to cremation place", "text": "This temple is only allowed for Hindus to enter, others can only view it from afar. It's right next to the funeral home of Kathmandu where you may see deceased being cremated. Please try not to take pictures to respect the family members of the deceased.\nBut it's an UNESCO site. \n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2013-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AA5B3A36FD3681597940CD902914C6CB", "name": "Geminican", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Geminican", "username": "Geminican", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/b8/default-avatar-2020-22.jpg", "contribution_count": 2147, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 33020, "location_name": "San Jose", "location_name_detailed": "San Jose, California"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2013-04-22", "published_at_date": "2013-04-21"}, {"review_id": 158396286, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158396286-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Touching place", "text": "The Pashupatinath Temple is one of the most sacred and important Hindu temples in the world and dedicated to Lord Shiva. The temple is located on the banks of the Bagmati River and you could get a good feel of Hindu traditions and culture there. You can find a little pagoda town full of monkeys running around but I felt a bit uncomfortable seeing the cremation ceremony from the other side of the holy Bagmati River....", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2013-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "37CFEB8C81087A424A8F8D5902D7EDB1", "name": "WaveriderBerlin", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/WaveriderBerlin", "username": "WaveriderBerlin", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/5a/default-avatar-2020-36.jpg", "contribution_count": 224, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/57/66/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/57/a4/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/57/df/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/58/19/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/58/52/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/cb/58/89/pashupatinath-tempel.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2013-04-21", "published_at_date": "2013-04-21"}, {"review_id": 158353282, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r158353282-Pashupa